{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/469105-pure-why-ripping-their-auspice-off-is-such-a-good-idea","id":469105,"title":"[Pure] Why ripping their Auspice off is such a good idea","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-04T20:25:17-07:00","id":469105,"title":"[Pure] Why ripping their Auspice off is such a good idea","content":"I've recently started a personal quest to find coherence and verisimilitude in the Pure ethos, stemming from its 1ed core book depiction and evolving into its more nuanced incarnation in The Pure and WtF2E.<br /> <br /> Now, I'm mostly sold on why the Pure Tribes are an engaging and compelling antagonists of the Forsaken, I really do. There's just this little aspect of Pure life that I cannot comprehend nor colate from their individual tribes' agenda: Why is so important to get rid of auspices in order to fulfill the Pure agenda. <br /> <br /> Of course I find the mythological justification sound, yet it still is just a justification, not a genuine reason. Why they believe Luna is anathema to the Pure agenda? If Predator Kings long for a predator's paradise and the animal release of instincts, the Fire-Touched preach a gospel of enshrinement of the Hisil and its inhabitants, and the Ivory Claws try to breed a pure lineage unblemished of weakness, why do they think Luna is in any way opposed to that? It's not like she sends forth commands to the Forsaken in any capacity, nor the Lunes espouse any particular zeal regarding the balance between flesh and spirit that could lend credence to the Pure's rejection of Auspice. Not to mention the huge boons they're refusing just because they think it's beneath them.<br /> <br /> Maybe this aspect has been addressed before, or maybe I'm just misinformed, but I'd love to have your opinion in this matter.<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T20:54:04-07:00","id":469141,"title":"","content":"She cursed all Uratha with the bane of silver's touch. But she only lifted it from those who follow her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T21:03:21-07:00","id":469148,"title":"","content":"Being spiritually tied to Luna appears to be part of the mechanism by which the Lunes judge what is worthy of Renown, and therefore by implication is a channel through which Father Moon sees Earthly events; she can't see events that transpire in the (totally chthonic) Underworld, and his light is grounds enough for the Pure to call for ceremonies to be held out of her sight.<br /> <br /> You may recall that the Warden Moon is insane, contrary, and possessed of the ability to send relatively clear indications of &quot;problem areas&quot; via dreams to her Forsaken children, who will likely take issue with your mucking around in their neck of the woods.<br /> <br /> Basically it's similar to Demon's SOP of &quot;rip the wires off of your Cover if you don't want your brethren to immediately track you down and murderize you due to the Machine seeing everything you do.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T21:11:19-07:00","id":469150,"title":"","content":"I think it facilitates them being able to judge their own and reward Renown from their elders down in accordance with their cultural ethos, rather than being externally judged by Lunes in accordance with the Oath of the Moon, that they're not party to.<br /> <br /> It also might be a straight up requirement for Rabid/Dire/Silver Wolf for Tribal sponsorship, since they hate Luna, and they don't want their tribes having divided loyalties.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T21:27:45-07:00","id":469157,"title":"","content":"It's not a good idea. The Pure do a lot of foolish things in the name of ideological purity and tribalism. Coherence and verisimilitude in belief systems and cultures don't always go hand in hand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T00:27:11-07:00","id":469234,"title":"","content":"It's a rejection of the duties given to them by the Lunes, who always seem to show up and try to convince werewolves to keep apart the worlds of spirit and flesh, etc.. It's also an act of worship and sacrifice that further serves to put them in the pockets of their spirit lords - it depowers them, making them more reliant on their freakish totems and their society and their false ethos - sorta like how cult leaders in the real world take away your power and your freedom to control you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":286,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","user":"Christian A","date":". 04-05-2015, 05:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T03:47:32-07:00","id":469277,"title":"","content":"Plus &quot;under the spirits' thumb(like appendages)&quot; and &quot;being an Ithaeur&quot; don't exactly mix well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T12:36:40-07:00","id":470314,"title":"","content":"Right, I've finally got the chance of rereading my digital copy of The Pure, and together with the answers here, I've been able to assemble some thoughts on the matter:<br /> <br /> - Luna is not the God-Machine, no matter what the Pure may tell you. She does not spy on every single uratha, nor does she send its lunes to catch pure werewolves unaware.<br /> <br /> - Luna has an agenda, however, one apparently consistent with what Father Wolf did back I'm the ol' days: enforcing the Oath of the Moon, keeping the worlds of flesh and spirits from freely intermingling, and sponsoring the Forsaken. She does all this by sending her lunes to watch over the Uratha and stands as judges for proper behavior; that is, Renown brands. There's also the extra benefit of rewarding honorary rank to the uratha according to their achievements.<br /> <br /> - The Pure Tribes espouse a creed of hatred, channeled through their myths and directed against forsaken for not rejecting Luna's teachings and blessings. They are the sole inheritors of Urfarah's legacy, but that legacy is understood as protecting the Hisil from Mother Moon and its Forsaken enforcers.<br /> <br /> - The Pure ethos is one of hatred, but essentially is a tribal conflict stoked ablaze with religious fanatism, bigotry and normalized abuse. They don't really know when the fight started, but their fear of the Other and their supernatural rage is a prime fuel for this sort of hate culture to emerge.<br /> <br /> - The Pure Totems are not only powerful, but inscrutable beings that care only for obedience from their uratha. Thus, the pure gets assimilated into their totem's own court, albeit with the half-fleshed status of shock troops and enforcers of their masters' agenda.<br /> <br /> - The Pure's Firstborn are clearly antagonistic with Mother Luna, and so their powerful patronage demands a clear rejection of everything Mother Luna stands for.<br /> <br /> - As with many hate groups, their ideal future is a glorified past where everything was cleaner and better without their victims' presence corrupting it.<br /> <br /> I think I have a better grasp at the Pure now. Any thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T14:20:14-07:00","id":470356,"title":"","content":"That seems about right, but I'll point out due to the mythical nature of Urfarah, it's hard to tell if the Oath of the Moon is his idea. It isn't, after all, the Oath of Father Wolf. The Pure believe they swear that one. Plus while Luna isn't the God Machine, she is a vastly powerful being who is likely capable of seeing everything done under the moon. The Bale Hounds seem to believe this is so, which is why they enjoy the Eclipse gifts, one of which can blind a werewolf to Luna, causing them to lose access to auspice gifts and renown.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-06-2015, 05:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T16:46:41-07:00","id":470475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zooroos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/469105-pure-why-ripping-their-auspice-off-is-such-a-good-idea?p=470314#post470314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Luna is not the God-Machine, no matter what the Pure may tell you. She does not spy on every single uratha, nor does she send its lunes to catch pure werewolves unaware.</div> </div> </div> </div>Setting aside the push to extremity that this represents in relation to my point of comparison and adding to the points already raised by nofather, I invite you to read the description of the Rite of the Final Moonrise.<br /> <br /> Also, have a Dave from three years ago:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DaveB</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/default8029-2.html?g=posts&amp;m=1404533#post1404533\" target=\"_blank\">[Luna] has things that she wants</a>, things that a Spirit 7 archmage can provide. [\u2026] <b>Create moonlight in the Underworld so she can add it to her territories.</b><br /> [\u2026]<br /> You want to alter one of her Werewolves? Make her an <i>offer.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T20:15:33-07:00","id":470712,"title":"","content":"Satchel, where can I find this rite you mentioned?<br /> <br /> Also, that comment from DaveB is very interesting. Thanks for bringing it up!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T21:31:02-07:00","id":470856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zooroos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/469105-pure-why-ripping-their-auspice-off-is-such-a-good-idea?p=470712#post470712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Satchel, where can I find this rite you mentioned?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's in <i>The Pure.</i> Page 128, though the salient portion of the rite straddles the border into page 129.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T17:32:29-07:00","id":475094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zooroos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/469105-pure-why-ripping-their-auspice-off-is-such-a-good-idea?p=470712#post470712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Satchel, where can I find this rite you mentioned?<br /> <br /> Also, that comment from DaveB is very interesting. Thanks for bringing it up!</div> </div> </div> </div>Essentially what it does, if you haven't already read it, is that it turns the willing Uratha participant into a living creature of silver. Fatal to the one who undergoes the transformation, but on the plus side it turns him/her into a perfect weapon to slaughter other werewolves for the amount of time they have left available.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T02:50:47-07:00","id":475568,"title":"","content":"I've just read the rite Satchel mentioned, but the part relevant to this conversation is the one which describes how performing the rite attracts the Lunes, who will try to attack the rite master. However, I still think that trying to come with a parallelism between Mother Moon and the God-Machine is misleading, in the same sense as using the Apocalypse mindset in Forsaken is misleading too.<br /> <br /> Both Luna and the God-Machine are ancient, all-powerful beings with a supernatural agenda and hosts of agents, servants and allies. But while the G-M doesn't tolerate dissidents nor deviations to its scheduled plans, Luna stands as a moral judge, enforcing proper behavior and denying unworthy Uratha of their blessings. <br /> <br /> The G-M is a primordial monster because it enforces a hands-on tiranny of amoral and unknowable workings. Against it, the Demons are clearly the underdogs and the oppressed minority, chased and forcibly reprogrammed when captured.<br /> <br /> The Moon Goddess looks for a higher moral ground. Their agenda, at least regarding the Uratha, is straightforward and clear, and doesn't actively chase down naysayers and unbelievers, they are just left out of the reinforcing loop. Against her, the Pure stands as bigoted and hateful, and their reasoning leaks from many holes, trying to paint themselves as justified in their hatred towards the Forsaken.<br /> <br /> Now, that's not to say that Father Luna is morally &quot;good&quot; in any capacity. She is still an alien being that sponsors a savage ecology of tooth and claw, and keeps the worlds of flesh and spirit from mixing too much. But clearly, their opposition is many shades darker and brutal, which works exactly as intended for the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":216,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","user":"Zooroos","date":". 04-10-2015, 05:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T05:06:27-07:00","id":475640,"title":"","content":"The comparison between Luna and the God Machine wasn't originally made about their morality or lack thereof, it was about their omnipresence and willingness to act.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zooroos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/469105-pure-why-ripping-their-auspice-off-is-such-a-good-idea?p=470314#post470314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Luna is not the God-Machine, no matter what the Pure may tell you. She does not spy on every single uratha, nor does she send its lunes to catch pure werewolves unaware.</div> </div> </div> </div>But we've established through this rite that Luna does pay attention to the Pure and what they do, and if they do something she really has a problem with, she will send her Lunes after the Pure.<br /> <br /> Also, while I'll grant that I haven't read much about the God Machine itself, Luna isn't exactly hands off. She has the Oath of the Moon, and legions of Uratha to follow them and do her bidding. The Pure seem more analogous to the Demons in this situation, except instead of Hell you have Paradise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-10-2015, 08:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T07:58:11-07:00","id":475831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/469105-pure-why-ripping-their-auspice-off-is-such-a-good-idea?p=475640#post475640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The comparison between Luna and the God Machine wasn't originally made about their morality or lack thereof, it was about their omnipresence and willingness to act.</div> </div> </div> </div> On that much we agree, certainly.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/469105-pure-why-ripping-their-auspice-off-is-such-a-good-idea?p=475640#post475640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, while I'll grant that I haven't read much about the God Machine itself, Luna isn't exactly hands off. She has the Oath of the Moon, and legions of Uratha to follow them and do her bidding. The Pure seem more analogous to the Demons in this situation, except instead of Hell you have Paradise.</div> </div> </div> </div> Sorry, but again this seems too much of a stretch to me. The analogy falls short when you consider that Mother Moon doesn't wage war against the Pure, not per default at least. She also doesn't send the lunes to attack the Pure except in rare occasions, like the rite of the final moonrise. The Pure, on the other hand, explicitly make war against the forsaken, kidnap and torture lunes when they think they can get away with it, do the same to humans and wolf-blooded as just another tactic of their war, and they become subservient to their spirits totem while accusing the Forsaken of being willing slaves to Luna. <br /> <br /> Trying to bring sympathy to the Pure goes only so far before starting to fall apart at the seams. Individually, the Pure may be looked at with a sympathetic eye, but collectively? They are assholes.<br /> <br /> We can respectfully agree to disagree however, YMMV after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T09:09:02-07:00","id":475915,"title":"","content":"She doesn't need to send the lunes to attack the Pure all the time, because she has Forsaken who can do that. While in the present, in the books, the Forsaken are on the rise and the Pure are getting sluggish after a big win from the Brethren War, its remarked in a few different places that the change is cyclical, and when the Forsaken gain the advantage of numbers they're pretty merciless with the Pure. But that might just be rhetoric.<br /> <br /> But just for clarification's sake it's the Bale Hounds that kidnap and torture lunes. There's at least one Pure pack in the books that has a lune-based magath as a totem. They even attempt to reach a middle ground. From the Pure, p185, ' The Silver Rush is a pack renowned in Anshega-controlled New Mexico as idealistic seekers, hunting after a better relationship with Luna and her Lunes, but without ever bending knee to her as the Forsaken do. The packmembers recognize her power, but they also recognize her insanity.'<br /> <br /> I didn't say that anyone should have sympathy for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-10-2015, 12:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T09:36:02-07:00","id":475938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zooroos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/469105-pure-why-ripping-their-auspice-off-is-such-a-good-idea?p=475568#post475568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've just read the rite Satchel mentioned, but the part relevant to this conversation is the one which describes how performing the rite attracts the Lunes, who will try to attack the rite master.</div> </div> </div> </div>If performed by <i>a werewolf with an auspice</i>, notably. Within <i>moments.</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However, I still think that trying to come with a parallelism between Mother Moon and the God-Machine is misleading, in the same sense as using the Apocalypse mindset in Forsaken is misleading too. </div> </div> </div>I have played exactly nothing of Apocalypse and read only marginally more of it. For contrast, I've comprehensively read all of Forsaken 1e along with Promethean 1e and Geist 1e within the last three years and am at least passingly familiar with concepts in every other published nWoD 1e gameline. I didn't come up with this comparison on a lark.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Against it, the Demons are clearly the underdogs and the oppressed minority, chased and forcibly reprogrammed when captured. </div> </div> </div>Demons cannot be remade into angels, are only given priority attention when they become a problem or necessary to a plan, and are occasionally stuck taking orders from loyal and/or mad angels in the very occurrences which most directly discourage them from banding together into large organized groups.<br /> <br /> I'm aware that demons aren't werewolves. My point of comparison was &quot;the Pure and the Unchained have both disconnected themselves from a unifying supernatural category whose overseer can exploit their association with it as a matter of policy.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Against her, the Pure stands as bigoted and hateful, and their reasoning leaks from many holes, trying to paint themselves as justified in their hatred towards the Forsaken. </div> </div> </div>There are demons who want to destroy reality without the excuse of being bound to beings that embody literal millennia of monomaniacal hatred. Culture is a distinct step from metaphysical alteration here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But clearly, their opposition is many shades darker and brutal, which works exactly as intended for the game. </div> </div> </div>As highlighted, I'm not sure what you think this has to do with anything about their capabilities and the behavior of their opposition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 04-10-2015, 12:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T12:32:51-07:00","id":476203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/469105-pure-why-ripping-their-auspice-off-is-such-a-good-idea?p=475938#post475938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Demons cannot be remade into angels, are only given priority attention when they become a problem or necessary to a plan, and are occasionally stuck taking orders from loyal and/or mad angels in the very occurrences which most directly discourage them from banding together into large organized groups.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Incorrect, the God-Machine has facilities dedicated recycling and rebuilding demons into angels. Dark Eras shows us a particularly terrifying example of such a facility in Berlin during the Cold War, if you feel like reading. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 04-10-2015, 03:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T12:54:19-07:00","id":476214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/469105-pure-why-ripping-their-auspice-off-is-such-a-good-idea?p=476203#post476203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incorrect, the God-Machine has facilities dedicated recycling and rebuilding demons into angels. Dark Eras shows us a particularly terrifying example of such a facility in Berlin during the Cold War, if you feel like reading.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where did you find that portion of Dark Eras?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T13:18:34-07:00","id":476231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/469105-pure-why-ripping-their-auspice-off-is-such-a-good-idea?p=476214#post476214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where did you find that portion of Dark Eras?</div> </div> </div> </div>Some time ago they released a google doc, I'm not sure if it's still around, but anyway it was in the demon section of the book","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T13:53:22-07:00","id":476260,"title":"","content":"Yeah, just like they did with Demon, they put up a Google doc containing the complete text of the book (minus the additional content that got added on in stretch goals obviously, since they hadn't been written yet) without any images or formatting, and linked to it from the kickstarter page. Not sure if it's still up, but I wouldn't be surprised if it was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T14:26:42-07:00","id":476277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/469105-pure-why-ripping-their-auspice-off-is-such-a-good-idea?p=476260#post476260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, just like they did with Demon, they put up a Google doc containing the complete text of the book (minus the additional content that got added on in stretch goals obviously, since they hadn't been written yet) without any images or formatting, and linked to it from the kickstarter page. Not sure if it's still up, but I wouldn't be surprised if it was.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you have any favorite parts in particular? Mine had to be the Dust Bowl with the Hollows","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T15:12:49-07:00","id":476335,"title":"","content":"Luna's main focus is on keeping alien spirit entities from entering Earth's Shadow. That some of here children aren't fulfilling their duties is an issue to her, but she has the rest of her kids to deal with that. And her various spirit choirs see that her will on that matter is reinforced. Besides, she already cursed them, and in 1e Pure suffered even more problems with Silver than Forsaken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T15:29:25-07:00","id":476353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/469105-pure-why-ripping-their-auspice-off-is-such-a-good-idea?p=476277#post476277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did you have any favorite parts in particular? Mine had to be the Dust Bowl with the Hollows</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I actually didn't read much of it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T16:24:38-07:00","id":476380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/469105-pure-why-ripping-their-auspice-off-is-such-a-good-idea?p=476203#post476203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Incorrect, the God-Machine has facilities dedicated recycling and rebuilding demons into angels. Dark Eras shows us a particularly terrifying example of such a facility in Berlin during the Cold War, if you feel like reading.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yah, in fact there is a whole Agenda that wishes to be re assimilated into the G-M, with fantasies of being rewarded some form of individuality for their loyalty. Even scarier, they tend to betray other demons to the G-M, in an attempt to &quot;save&quot; their fallen brothers. So those other demons you clicked with? Can't trust them brah!<br /> <br /> Feeds into the paranoia of the game.<br /> <br /> Being turned back into an angel of the G-M is one of the most terrible endings for a demon. And your buddy might be the one to serve you on a silver platter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T16:44:27-07:00","id":476396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/469105-pure-why-ripping-their-auspice-off-is-such-a-good-idea?p=476380#post476380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yah, in fact there is a whole Agenda that wishes to be re assimilated into the G-M, with fantasies of being rewarded some form of individuality for their loyalty. Even scarier, they tend to betray other demons to the G-M, in an attempt to &quot;save&quot; their fallen brothers. So those other demons you clicked with? Can't trust them brah!<br /> <br /> Feeds into the paranoia of the game.<br /> <br /> Being turned back into an angel of the G-M is one of the most terrible endings for a demon. And your buddy might be the one to serve you on a silver platter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh he knows about that, or at least I hope he does, otherwise I question how he knows so much about Intergrators if that isn't the case lol.<br /> <br /> playful jabbing at Satch aside; there are a few parallels between the Unchained and the Anshega, but in a way that reminds me of how Changeling and Geist are similar due to characters having to travel through nigh-endless maze realms and have interesting relations with Fate. They have similarities, but are still very different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T16:45:39-07:00","id":476397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/469105-pure-why-ripping-their-auspice-off-is-such-a-good-idea?p=476353#post476353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I actually didn't read much of it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Oh noes!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T16:56:53-07:00","id":476428,"title":"","content":"Don't Demons have a version of Paradise or something, too?<br /> <br /> I'm so horrible. All these kickstarters and I haven't been able to use anything from them. The players didn't go after the mummy trap, the demon was passed off quickly to an NPC, we haven't touched classic World of Darkness. I am managing to win them over on the idea of a historical game, and I think I could lure them into VtM to take advantage of v20 Dark Ages whenever we get a chance. But I'm really enjoying Werewolf so I'm in no rush.<br /> <br /> I know you didn't ask me, Kogora, and this is obviously derailing, but my favorite chapters so far were Doubting Souls, then Requiem for Regina. To re-rail things, I'm really excited about all the Werewolf content, and I think it will be interesting to see if they depict times when the Forsaken were large and in charge and how they acted towards the Pure. Plus, Neolithic Werewolf. Did they get along before they were tribes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T17:16:12-07:00","id":476457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/469105-pure-why-ripping-their-auspice-off-is-such-a-good-idea?p=476428#post476428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't Demons have a version of Paradise or something, too?<br /> <br /> I'm so horrible. All these kickstarters and I haven't been able to use anything from them. The players didn't go after the mummy trap, the demon was passed off quickly to an NPC, we haven't touched classic World of Darkness. I am managing to win them over on the idea of a historical game, and I think I could lure them into VtM to take advantage of v20 Dark Ages whenever we get a chance. But I'm really enjoying Werewolf so I'm in no rush.<br /> <br /> I know you didn't ask me, Kogora, and this is obviously derailing, but my favorite chapters so far were Doubting Souls, then Requiem for Regina. To re-rail things, I'm really excited about all the Werewolf content, and I think it will be interesting to see if they depict times when the Forsaken were large and in charge and how they acted towards the Pure. Plus, Neolithic Werewolf. Did they get along before they were tribes?</div> </div> </div> </div>They have Hell, but each Hell is unique to the individual Demon, and it can apparently be anything from simply a sort of inner peace ( and invisibility regarding the God-Machine and it's slaves) to a seperate universe ruled by the demon to the neighborhood that the demon lives in. Whatever Hell may be, the specifics don't matter, all that matters is that the Demon has achieved complete separation from the God-Machine.'<br /> <br /> And I was rather fond of the Changeling chapter, and the Geist chapter.<br /> <br /> Back on topic, I am rather excited about that too.. though I have little to know interest in Neolithic mage. Ancient werewolves are awesome, but with everything that has been disclosed about Mage 2nd ed has either made me sad, mad, or completely disinterested.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 04-10-2015, 08:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T20:39:55-07:00","id":476569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/469105-pure-why-ripping-their-auspice-off-is-such-a-good-idea?p=476203#post476203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Incorrect, the God-Machine has facilities dedicated <b>recycling and rebuilding</b> demons into angels.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you pay close attention, you'll notice that this is not the same thing as turning a demon into an angel and in fact is almost the entire reason why the Idealists exist as a faction at all rather than simply throwing themselves back into the furnace.<br /> <br /> My point in bringing <b>that</b> up, to wind things back, is that tearing out your auspice is irreversible and only works if you're &quot;willing&quot; at the moment it occurs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 04-10-2015, 11:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T20:41:52-07:00","id":476571,"title":"","content":"So it's less a Lodge of Salvation-like conversion and more of a taking you apart until those parts need to be used again?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T09:48:17-07:00","id":477058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/469105-pure-why-ripping-their-auspice-off-is-such-a-good-idea?p=476569#post476569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you pay close attention, you'll notice that this is not the same thing as turning a demon into an angel and in fact is almost the entire reason why the Idealists exist as a faction at all rather than simply throwing themselves back into the furnace.<br /> <br /> My point in bringing <b>that</b> up, to wind things back, is that tearing out your auspice is irreversible and only works if you're &quot;willing&quot; at the moment it occurs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again that's also incorrect.. well you're correct about one thing. Their aetheric superstructure is rebuilt into a angel who is once again a fully techno-ephemeral entity and possessed of all the same in-built systems of control every other loyalist has, they return to being an angel in every single way. which is why the Idealists are so frightened about just letting themselves become what they used to be. They want to be in God's embrace yes, but on their own terms, they want true free will- free will and unthinking obedience do not mix. So in reality an Intergrator's goal is much more complicated and different than simply being recast as a angel.<br /> <br /> So about the Idealists, you're right on the money, just not so much on the process of recycling. Yes the particular personality of that individual demon is either burned away or otherwise lost, but the preservation of the demon is not the goal of the God-Machine- recovering and restoring/recycling a servant and piece of property is the MO in this situation.<br /> <br /> But you made your point, it is a incredibly painful and ultimately willful action to remove the Auspice, ill-fitting comparisons with demons aside.<br /> <br /> Now interestingly enough, WAtP does allude to Luna having the ability to forcibly re-instilling Auspice on unwilling Pure.. though it's described as being as bad, if not worse that the Rite of Blood and Silver.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 04-11-2015, 01:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T09:54:02-07:00","id":477061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/469105-pure-why-ripping-their-auspice-off-is-such-a-good-idea?p=476571#post476571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it's less a Lodge of Salvation-like conversion and more of a taking you apart until those parts need to be used again?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the Lodge of Salvation doesn't offer true forgiveness, &quot;salvation&quot; for it's Pure converts. So yeah, though that &quot;new&quot; angel can always fall as well XD<br /> <br /> &quot;What rises may fall. What has fallen may rise again.&quot; The horror of those words is worse than one would imagine at first.<br /> <br /> Which is why I like the Unchained addendum to that statement xD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T10:55:08-07:00","id":477086,"title":"","content":"Why are we discussing Descent here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T11:04:20-07:00","id":477092,"title":"","content":"The parallels between Demons and the Pure, and Angels and the Forsaken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T11:07:39-07:00","id":477099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/469105-pure-why-ripping-their-auspice-off-is-such-a-good-idea?p=477092#post477092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The parallels between Demons and the Pure, and Angels and the Forsaken.</div> </div> </div> </div>And, to a more direct extent, the parallels between auspice-as-connection-to-Luna and connection to the Machine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T12:08:31-07:00","id":477156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/469105-pure-why-ripping-their-auspice-off-is-such-a-good-idea?p=477099#post477099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And, to a more direct extent, the parallels between auspice-as-connection-to-Luna and connection to the Machine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Though those parallels are admittedly not that terribly strong, seeing as Luna is even more distant than the God-Machine even with a connection to her children... though to be perfectly honest, she still has a connection to the Pure even without Auspice, as they are still of her and Urfarah's &quot;flesh&quot; so to speak. Still, the Pure do share the hatred and fear of an all powerful parent like Demons do, so close enough right? lol.<br /> <br /> Huh, maybe the Pure and Demons are exactly the same after all. Good talk Satch!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 04-11-2015, 03:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T12:32:47-07:00","id":477164,"title":"","content":"And they remove their Auspice for a similar reason to why demons usually supplement or burn their first cover. Among other reasons, of course. But that parallel was what triggered this line of conversation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}